# The measured revision: what `result-v2/INDEX.md` measures staleness against and
# what `scripts/setup_extern_deps.sh` materialises as `extern/cpueinsum-rs`.
#
# `cpueinsum-rs` main `1030db3` ("cpueinsum-bench: the timing-v2 harness over the
# einsum instance corpus (#27)") is the revision that first carries the harness this
# campaign measures with: the `crates/cpueinsum-bench` crate (binary
# `cpueinsum-bench`, the `run|verify|info` timing-v2 contract with a verification
# census, chronological samples, rotated execution order and observed thread
# readback). Its tree is identical to the reviewed branch head `3278a1a`; the merge
# is what this pin names because that is what a reader can fetch by revision.
# `v0.2.1` from 2026-10-19: the pin moves from 1030db32 to the released tag, the version
# the campaign's pages should describe.
# `main` (5f8820f) from 2026-10-19: the newest revision that carries the harness. The
# last release tag `v0.2.1` (5ad1257) is an ancestor of the previous pin `1030db32` and
# predates `crates/cpueinsum-bench`, so pinning it would remove the harness the campaign
# builds out of the measured checkout. `main` is five commits past the old pin and still
# carries it.
5f8820f4f8200522939511afbee26c3ddc7ad934
